isOver() compares the current state against GameOverState.getInstance() using ==, not equals(). Why is reference comparison correct here?,It is not correct - equals() should be used and this is a bug,"Because GameOverState is a singleton: exactly one instance exists, so a game is over precisely when its state field points at that one object",Because IGameState does not declare equals(),Because == is faster than equals() for interfaces,,2,"Singleton states make identity comparison meaningful. If states were created with 'new' each time, == would fail and every state class would need its own equals().",2

