public boolean isOver() { return state == GameOverState.getInstance(); }

You want to add a REPLAY condition in which move() is ignored but the board can still be read. Which of these are needed? (select all that apply),A new ReplayState class implementing IGameState,Something that calls game.setState(ReplayState.getInstance()),"Edits to RunningState, PausedState and GameOverState",A new method on the IGameState interface,An if/else added to SnakeGame.move(),"1,2","The three existing states, the interface and the three entry points are untouched. Adding a condition costs one new class plus a way to enter it.",2

