public class PausedState implements IGameState {

    @Override
    public void move(SnakeGame game, Direction direction) {
        throw new InvalidMoveException("cannot move while paused");
    }

    @Override
    public void pause(SnakeGame game) {
        throw new InvalidMoveException("game is already paused");
    }

    @Override
    public void resume(SnakeGame game) {
        game.setState(RunningState.getInstance());
    }
}

PausedState.pause() throws "game is already paused" rather than doing nothing. A caller pausing an already-paused game arguably got what they wanted. Is throwing right here?,"Yes, always - repeating any operation must be an error",It is defensible either way. Throwing surfaces a caller who has lost track of the game's condition

