In the recorded run, the snake died on step 29 attempting to move LEFT from (4,4) into (4,3), which its own body occupied. Afterwards getHead() still reported (4,4), not (4,3). Why?,getHead() has an off-by-one error,"The collision was detected before any mutation - performMove() calls endGame() and returns before body.addFirst(newHead) ever runs, so the illegal position is never written into the snake",The head was moved and then rolled back after the collision check,"(4,3) was outside the board so the position was discarded",,2,"The rejected move leaves no trace at all. The snake did not die AT (4,3) - it never went there
